  - metro manila
  - civic technology
abstract: >
  undercover.ph finds walking routes in 14 areas of Metro Manila that cut time in
  the sun on sunny days and time outside cover when it rains. It is a Philippine
  take on Singapore's Undercover prototype. It casts shadows on each sidewalk edge
  every 30 minutes, from OpenStreetMap and Google Open Buildings heights and a tree
  canopy height raster. A custom A* search in the browser returns the shortest,
  the most covered, and a recommended route. Paths that may be gated or private,
  closed mall passages, and mid-block road crossings stay out of routes. The shade
  values come from a model. Nobody checked them in the field yet.
